1
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:08,767
Welcome to Adyru OS.

2
00:00:08,917 --> 00:00:13,257
In this guide, you'll learn how to run
an entire company from one place,

3
00:00:13,297 --> 00:00:17,707
with a team of AI agents doing the
work, and you making the decisions.

4
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,291
We'll go step by step.

5
00:00:19,601 --> 00:00:22,480
First, signing in and finding your way around.

6
00:00:22,746 --> 00:00:26,774
Then, giving the company a goal, and
approving what your agents prepare.

7
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:31,196
And finally, a tour of every
department, from sales and marketing,

8
00:00:31,236 --> 00:00:33,577
to finance, operations and security.

9
00:00:33,948 --> 00:00:37,600
Everything you'll see runs on
demo data, so after watching,

10
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:40,361
feel free to click around and
explore on your own.

11
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:48,793
To get started, open your Adyru link and sign
in with the username and password you

12
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:53,710
were given. Your access is personal,
so please keep it to yourself.

13
00:00:54,113 --> 00:00:57,038
Once you're signed in, you
land on Mission Control,

14
00:00:57,113 --> 00:00:58,321
your home page.

15
00:01:02,167 --> 00:01:03,889
Let's take a quick look around.

16
00:01:04,032 --> 00:01:08,499
On the left is the sidebar,
grouped by what you want to do.

17
00:01:08,552 --> 00:01:12,005
Work, for your inbox, tasks and goals.

18
00:01:12,045 --> 00:01:15,524
Team, for your AI agents and
the company's knowledge.

19
00:01:15,564 --> 00:01:17,920
Grow, for sales, marketing and insights.

20
00:01:17,998 --> 00:01:19,734
And Money, for finance.

21
00:01:19,992 --> 00:01:23,686
Across the top, you'll find
the company switcher,

22
00:01:23,826 --> 00:01:28,197
a search bar, the Demo data badge that
reminds you nothing here is real,

23
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:31,418
help, the light and dark theme
switch, your notifications,

24
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:32,928
and your profile.

25
00:01:33,967 --> 00:01:37,568
At the bottom of the sidebar is
the Simple and Pro switch.

26
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:41,885
Simple keeps things calm, and shows
what most people need every day.

27
00:01:42,238 --> 00:01:45,997
Pro reveals every department
and every advanced tool.

28
00:01:46,347 --> 00:01:49,651
We'll stay in Simple for now,
and switch to Pro later on.

29
00:01:50,055 --> 00:01:54,270
The first time you open Adyru, a small
card offers a one minute tour,

30
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:58,981
or a guided setup. You can bring
both back at any time from Help.

31
00:02:02,833 --> 00:02:05,074
Mission Control is your home page.

32
00:02:05,179 --> 00:02:08,794
It shows today's date, how many
agents are working right now,

33
00:02:08,886 --> 00:02:13,050
how many decisions are waiting for you,
and how many tasks are in flight.

34
00:02:13,346 --> 00:02:16,575
The most important box on this
page asks one simple question.

35
00:02:16,615 --> 00:02:18,972
What do you want to get done?

36
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:21,459
Type a goal in plain English.

37
00:02:21,509 --> 00:02:22,933
One sentence is enough.

38
00:02:23,131 --> 00:02:24,748
Then send it to the Brain.

39
00:02:25,110 --> 00:02:28,675
Atlas, the company's lead
agent, turns it into a plan,

40
00:02:28,715 --> 00:02:30,280
splits it into tasks, hands
them to the right agents,

41
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:34,847
and comes back to you before
anything sensitive happens.

42
00:02:35,049 --> 00:02:36,201
Not sure what to write?

43
00:02:36,373 --> 00:02:38,636
Just click one of the suggestions underneath.

44
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:42,938
Below that, two guided paths
help you get going:

45
00:02:43,117 --> 00:02:47,283
From idea to published post, and
Run my company this week.

46
00:02:47,323 --> 00:02:50,464
Each one shows its steps and
how far you've got.

47
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:55,379
Further down, Needs your decision lists the
actions waiting for your approval,

48
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:58,330
with Approve and Reject
right there on the card.

49
00:02:58,551 --> 00:03:02,138
And Agents at work shows
which teams are busiest,

50
00:03:02,178 --> 00:03:03,434
live, as it happens.

51
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:10,904
Before we move on, here's a
shortcut you'll use every day.

52
00:03:11,237 --> 00:03:16,167
Press Control and K, or click the search
bar, to open the command palette.

53
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:20,234
Start typing, and you can jump
to any page, find a task,

54
00:03:20,274 --> 00:03:23,991
a goal, an agent or a
document, or run a command,

55
00:03:24,031 --> 00:03:25,653
without touching the menu.

56
00:03:25,928 --> 00:03:29,258
Use the arrow keys to move, and Enter to open.

57
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:38,094
Next, the Inbox. This is where
everything that needs a person ends up.

58
00:03:38,487 --> 00:03:42,703
The first tab, Approvals, holds the
actions your agents have prepared,

59
00:03:42,743 --> 00:03:45,874
but are not allowed to do on their own.

60
00:03:45,914 --> 00:03:49,614
Payments, invoices, ledger
postings, external emails,

61
00:03:49,654 --> 00:03:54,043
deploys, and more. This is the heart of
how Adyru keeps you in control.

62
00:03:54,339 --> 00:03:56,693
Agents never approve their own work.

63
00:03:56,930 --> 00:04:02,591
Anything that spends money, publishes,
sends something outside the company,

64
00:04:02,678 --> 00:04:04,514
signs, or deletes, waits here for a human.

65
00:04:05,567 --> 00:04:08,545
Each card shows the risk
level, the department,

66
00:04:08,585 --> 00:04:11,443
the amount, and when the request expires.

67
00:04:11,723 --> 00:04:16,309
Click Show what will happen, to see
exactly what the agent will do,

68
00:04:16,622 --> 00:04:19,589
and why. Then approve it, or
reject it with a short reason,

69
00:04:19,629 --> 00:04:21,051
so the agent learns.

70
00:04:21,431 --> 00:04:25,401
The tabs at the top let you look
back at what was approved,

71
00:04:25,441 --> 00:04:30,502
executed, rejected or expired, so there's
always a clear record of who decided what.

72
00:04:31,567 --> 00:04:35,538
The Messages tab brings every
customer channel into one place:

73
00:04:35,702 --> 00:04:39,545
email, web chat, WhatsApp,
Telegram, Instagram,

74
00:04:39,585 --> 00:04:44,575
Facebook and SMS. Agents draft
replies in your brand voice.

75
00:04:44,741 --> 00:04:48,718
Anything they're unsure about waits for you,
and conversations that are about to

76
00:04:48,758 --> 00:04:51,539
miss their response time are flagged in red.

77
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:59,020
Under Tasks and goals, you can
follow the work itself.

78
00:04:59,248 --> 00:05:02,809
Tasks shows what each agent is
working on, its status,

79
00:05:02,849 --> 00:05:06,849
its priority, and what it has
cost in AI usage so far.

80
00:05:07,099 --> 00:05:10,559
Switch between the list and the
board, or filter by status,

81
00:05:10,599 --> 00:05:12,364
department or agent.

82
00:05:12,555 --> 00:05:16,574
A task only counts as done once
its result has been verified.

83
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:20,906
Goals are the outcomes you've
asked the company to deliver,

84
00:05:20,956 --> 00:05:24,423
like closing the month's books,
or launching a new product.

85
00:05:24,759 --> 00:05:28,087
Each card shows its progress,
how many tasks are done,

86
00:05:28,127 --> 00:05:31,162
running, or waiting for
approval, and the due date.

87
00:05:31,557 --> 00:05:35,594
Create a new goal right here, or
simply type it into Mission Control.

88
00:05:39,433 --> 00:05:41,707
Now, let's meet your AI team.

89
00:05:41,973 --> 00:05:45,125
The org chart shows every
agent, who they report to,

90
00:05:45,165 --> 00:05:46,517
and what they cost.

91
00:05:46,767 --> 00:05:50,894
At the top is Atlas, the Brain,
supported by an executive assistant,

92
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:53,994
and an independent quality
team that checks the work.

93
00:05:54,472 --> 00:05:58,693
Below them, each department has a head
agent who leads a group of specialists.

94
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:03,048
Click any agent to read their job, the
tools they're allowed to use,

95
00:06:03,088 --> 00:06:04,604
and their recent work.

96
00:06:05,667 --> 00:06:09,957
Switch the view to Marketing team, to see
a complete marketing department:

97
00:06:10,165 --> 00:06:12,446
fifty roles in ten teams.

98
00:06:12,710 --> 00:06:16,427
Market intelligence, strategy
and positioning, search,

99
00:06:16,467 --> 00:06:20,960
content, social, demand
generation, email and lifecycle,

100
00:06:21,009 --> 00:06:24,279
conversion, analytics, and
marketing operations.

101
00:06:24,619 --> 00:06:29,288
Every role has a clear job, and anything
that would publish or spend money still

102
00:06:29,328 --> 00:06:30,994
waits for your approval.

103
00:06:32,033 --> 00:06:36,901
In Team builder, you can draw your own
agent team like an org chart,

104
00:06:36,945 --> 00:06:39,101
try it out, then publish it.

105
00:06:39,141 --> 00:06:41,658
Or start from a ready made
team, such as finance,

106
00:06:41,698 --> 00:06:43,767
sales, marketing or social media.

107
00:06:44,196 --> 00:06:48,684
Missions are your always-on agents:
standing jobs that run in the background,

108
00:06:48,724 --> 00:06:51,061
like watching your inbox or your cash.

109
00:06:51,341 --> 00:06:54,511
The console shows what they did,
what needs your attention,

110
00:06:54,551 --> 00:06:57,546
and what they spent.

111
00:06:57,586 --> 00:07:01,854
And if you ever need to, the red Stop
everything button pauses every agent at once.

112
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:08,606
Brain and knowledge is the company's memory.

113
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:11,843
On the Brain tab, you can
talk to Atlas directly.

114
00:07:12,034 --> 00:07:14,948
Give it a goal, or ask about
anything in the company.

115
00:07:15,179 --> 00:07:18,845
It answers with the real status of
the work, who owns each piece,

116
00:07:18,885 --> 00:07:21,258
and exactly what it needs from you.

117
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:25,253
Company Brain shows
everything the company knows,

118
00:07:25,293 --> 00:07:29,940
and who added it: notes,
customers, content and decisions,

119
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:31,565
and how they all connect.

120
00:07:31,918 --> 00:07:37,354
Brand DNA holds the rules every new post,
ad and design is checked against,

121
00:07:37,394 --> 00:07:39,302
so everything sounds like you.

122
00:07:39,342 --> 00:07:43,965
You can also connect your other AI tools,
so they all share the same memory.

123
00:07:44,292 --> 00:07:48,019
Knowledge, Documents and Files
hold your source material.

124
00:07:51,867 --> 00:07:55,937
Now let's look at the Grow section,
starting with Sales and customers.

125
00:07:56,194 --> 00:08:00,774
The CRM shows your pipeline as a
board, from lead all the way to won,

126
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:02,715
with the value of each stage.

127
00:08:02,961 --> 00:08:07,478
Sales agents keep the next steps up to
date, but you decide what closes.

128
00:08:07,728 --> 00:08:12,264
Inside, you'll also find
quotes, products and pricing,

129
00:08:12,304 --> 00:08:16,844
forecasts, meetings, partners,
and the customer portal.

130
00:08:16,884 --> 00:08:20,486
The other tabs cover leads,
audiences, customers and contracts.

131
00:08:21,533 --> 00:08:25,845
Loyalty and pricing runs your
promotions, coupons,

132
00:08:25,885 --> 00:08:28,699
store credit, points,
referrals and price tests.

133
00:08:28,994 --> 00:08:33,554
Every balance is posted to the ledger, so what
you owe your customers always matches

134
00:08:33,594 --> 00:08:34,609
your books.

135
00:08:38,467 --> 00:08:40,786
Marketing is where content gets made.

136
00:08:40,971 --> 00:08:44,852
In the Studio, start a new draft,
pick a template and a channel,

137
00:08:44,892 --> 00:08:49,489
and write it yourself, or let an
agent write it for you.

138
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:52,274
The voice guard scores every draft
against your brand kit as you type.

139
00:08:52,598 --> 00:08:55,906
From here you can also build
landing pages, run experiments,

140
00:08:55,946 --> 00:08:57,920
and work on video and images.

141
00:08:58,081 --> 00:09:01,966
And as always, nothing goes out
without a person approving it.

142
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,471
Campaigns and Social plan and schedule
your posts across every channel.

143
00:09:07,789 --> 00:09:11,219
Ads brings your Google and Meta
results into one view,

144
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:14,583
with spend, conversions, and
return on ad spend.

145
00:09:14,947 --> 00:09:18,714
The Ad platform lets you sell
advertising on your own surfaces.

146
00:09:18,926 --> 00:09:21,923
And SEO checks your websites
for technical issues,

147
00:09:21,963 --> 00:09:24,409
and tracks how you rank in search.

148
00:09:28,267 --> 00:09:30,943
Insights turns your data into answers.

149
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:35,529
In Analytics, pick a dataset, choose
what to measure and how to group it,

150
00:09:35,569 --> 00:09:38,971
and the chart updates as you build.

151
00:09:39,011 --> 00:09:41,948
Save it as a report, or add it to a dashboard.

152
00:09:41,988 --> 00:09:44,107
The Insights tab answers
questions in plain language,

153
00:09:44,147 --> 00:09:47,157
and in Pro mode you also get
the full data platform,

154
00:09:47,197 --> 00:09:48,944
including experiments.

155
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:57,691
Now, Money. Finance is a complete
double-entry accounting system.

156
00:09:57,836 --> 00:10:01,259
You can see your cash across bank
accounts, profit and loss,

157
00:10:01,299 --> 00:10:04,382
what customers owe you,
what you owe suppliers,

158
00:10:04,422 --> 00:10:06,430
and your latest journal entries.

159
00:10:06,645 --> 00:10:09,984
Every posting is balanced, can't
be changed after the fact,

160
00:10:10,024 --> 00:10:11,469
and is fully audited.

161
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:15,004
Create an invoice or a journal entry
from the buttons at the top,

162
00:10:15,077 --> 00:10:19,100
and use the tabs for
accounts, invoices and bills,

163
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:21,732
banking, reports, and closing each period.

164
00:10:22,767 --> 00:10:27,093
The Finance team is a group of agents that
prepare the work of an entire finance

165
00:10:27,133 --> 00:10:31,294
function: reconciling bank
accounts, chasing invoices,

166
00:10:31,334 --> 00:10:35,387
preparing the month-end
close, and filing reports.

167
00:10:35,427 --> 00:10:37,529
You approve, they execute.

168
00:10:37,569 --> 00:10:40,617
You can ask the CFO agent a
question, read the daily brief,

169
00:10:40,657 --> 00:10:42,494
or explore what-if scenarios.

170
00:10:42,676 --> 00:10:45,848
And no agent can ever move money on its own.

171
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:53,204
Let's switch to Pro mode, to
reveal the Operate section.

172
00:10:53,459 --> 00:10:56,701
Operations covers the day-to-day
running of the business.

173
00:10:56,892 --> 00:11:00,128
Ops and engineering shows what
needs a person today:

174
00:11:00,168 --> 00:11:03,513
monitors that are down, open
incidents, code reviews,

175
00:11:03,553 --> 00:11:09,789
shipping labels and risky vendors, plus a
Reliability tab for uptime goals.

176
00:11:09,829 --> 00:11:13,434
Inventory, purchasing, projects and
product live right next to it.

177
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:18,758
If you run a marketplace, Dispatch
shows supply and demand live,

178
00:11:18,798 --> 00:11:21,964
with jobs, providers, and fair pricing caps.

179
00:11:22,204 --> 00:11:26,369
And Back office brings together
procurement, PR and communications,

180
00:11:26,409 --> 00:11:30,309
investor relations, business
development, learning,

181
00:11:30,349 --> 00:11:34,807
facilities, internal audit and user research,
each with its own agents and its own

182
00:11:34,847 --> 00:11:35,831
approvals.

183
00:11:39,667 --> 00:11:44,041
People handles leave,
attendance, goals, reviews,

184
00:11:44,112 --> 00:11:46,547
onboarding, and the company directory.

185
00:11:46,868 --> 00:11:52,249
Risk and compliance keeps contracts, privacy,
security readiness and policies in one

186
00:11:52,289 --> 00:11:54,777
place, with deadlines you won't miss.

187
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:59,095
Trust and safety scores risky
actions and keeps a review queue.

188
00:11:59,373 --> 00:12:03,424
The Security center watches
sign-ins, alerts and active sessions.

189
00:12:03,563 --> 00:12:06,318
And the Audit log records
every important action,

190
00:12:06,358 --> 00:12:08,599
by people and agents alike.

191
00:12:12,433 --> 00:12:16,671
Finally, Settings. This is where
you set up your organization,

192
00:12:16,711 --> 00:12:20,604
how much the AI may do on its
own, your approval policy,

193
00:12:20,644 --> 00:12:24,597
members and security, and the look of
the app, including white label,

194
00:12:24,637 --> 00:12:28,065
with your own name, logo and colors.

195
00:12:28,105 --> 00:12:32,563
Channels connects email and messaging,
Integrations connects the tools you already

196
00:12:32,603 --> 00:12:36,951
use, and the Developers area
manages your API keys and apps.

197
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:44,865
Adyru works beautifully on your phone, too.

198
00:12:44,905 --> 00:12:47,456
The layout adapts to any screen,
with a bottom bar for Home,

199
00:12:47,496 --> 00:12:50,250
Inbox, Ask, Work, and More.

200
00:12:50,290 --> 00:12:54,059
And you can switch between the dark
and light themes at any time.

201
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:57,584
And that's the full tour.

202
00:12:57,943 --> 00:13:00,203
To recap: tell Mission
Control what you want done,

203
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:04,991
let your agents prepare the work, and
approve what matters from your Inbox.

204
00:13:05,031 --> 00:13:08,187
Then explore each department at your own pace.

205
00:13:08,401 --> 00:13:13,460
Everything here runs on demo data,
so you can't break anything.

206
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,464
Thanks for watching, and enjoy Adyru OS.
